        {
          "id": 686757356,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "There was a Ask question about exporting HTTP without all the TCP overhead packets:   \nhttps://ask.wireshark.org/question/24428/export-selected-http-works-strange-got-another-tcp-packets/  \n  \nA filter like `tcp.reassembled_in == ${tcp.reassembled_in}` to select one and get a list of all including the last one.  \n  \n(sample capture [tcp-ethereal-file1.trace](/wireshark/wireshark/-/wikis/uploads/__moin_import__/attachments/SampleCaptures/tcp-ethereal-file1.trace) (libpcap) A large POST request, taking many TCP segments.)  \n\nIt's in the list of segments and doesn't stand alone - it's part of a reassembly.  \n  \n```\n[131 Reassembled TCP Segments (152996 bytes): #6(624), #7(836), #9(1260), #11(1260), #12(1260), #14(1260), #15(1260), #17(1056), #22(1260), #23(1260), #24(1260), #25(1260), #26(1260), #27(1260), #28(632), #36(1260), #37(1260), #38(1260), #3]\n    [Frame: 6, payload: 0-623 (624 bytes)]\n----  snip  ----\n    [Frame: 213, payload: 148080-149339 (1260 bytes)]\n    [Frame: 214, payload: 149340-150599 (1260 bytes)]\n    [Frame: 215, payload: 150600-151859 (1260 bytes)]\n    [Frame: 216, payload: 151860-152995 (1136 bytes)]\n    [Segment count: 131]\n    [Reassembled TCP length: 152996]\n    [Reassembled TCP Data: 504f5354202f657468657265616c2d6c6162732f6c6162332d312d7265706c792e68746d…]\n```  \n  \nThere is a test associated with `tcp.reassembled_in` that caused pipeline to fail - I need to update if the change (in concept) is accepted.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6701257,
            "username": "chuckcraft",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Chuck Craft",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0809ffc6d9d98013a1895132bc055c622830b8a20bfa49328f53d5eb4a1206cb?s=80&d=identicon",
