        {
          "id": 686800984,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Originally added here \nhttps://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/commit/f3d64a2c3834a26a87ec266a4397f43b21b62a70 Add a \"reassembled in\" field.  \n  \nThe field description has been updated slightly from the original. Now reads:  \n`\"The PDU that doesn't end in this segment is reassembled in this frame\"`\n  \nWhat is the purpose of excluding the last frame?  \n  \nI think this could be used to build a HTTP conversation for `Follow->HTTP Stream` instead of generating a filter for `tcp.stream` that includes a lot of non-HTTP packets. What is the definition of a `HTTP Stream`?",
          "author": {
            "id": 6701257,
            "username": "chuckcraft",
